Chapter 14
When all the sound goes quiet and I feel like I've stopped falling, I open my eyes.
(t): Huh? Everything is dark. In fact, it's pitch black. I can't see a thing.
I begin to question wether I really have my eyes open or not, but it stays the same, even after blinking a few times.
I try to reach for anything tangible in the darkness. It feels like I'm floating through empty space.
???: Stay still. You wont be able to see anything, only our eyes are able to see in this space.
(t): The Spirit from earlier!
Me: Where am I? What are you going to do to me now?
???: We are in the realm of the abyss where we, the Interdimensional Spirits, reside. It is also the place where we came up with our plan to unify all the dimensions.
(t): The realm of the abyss? Is this where they originate from?
???: Don't fret. Nothing will happen to you, as long as you agree to stay here and don't get in our way. We will make your stay here as comfortable as possible. You will not feel a thing.
Me: That sounds like you are going to put me into a coma.
The Spirit ignores my remark.
???: We will proceed to peacefully bring every universe into yours, it will serve as the main vessel. And, of course, your lover will remain untouched… By us.
(t): Something's fishy.
Me: Why did you say it like that? I don't see how you can make this sound so peaceful and harmless. Where's the catch?
I hear the voice cackle ominously.
???: WE won't be doing anything violent. We only wish to rule over the empire that our plan creates. To get there, we bring all the dimensions together, along with all the inhabitants.
Me: Why? Was the world not perfectly fine before?
???: You don't know anything. If all the universes unite, that means that all the powers and energies that exist out there unite as well. From there, it will be survival of the fittest and everything will sort itself into it's natural order.
Me: Natural? The state of only one universe existing is an artificial order, created by you and your other abyssal Spirits! You can't call that natural. And what you just said sounds like all the different inhabitants are going to get into one big massacre. I can't let you do that.
???: But don't you agree? One Dimension is far easier to oversee than multiple. It makes your work a little simpler, no?
(t): That bastard is still trying to gaslight me into thinking their plans are for the greater good.
Me: My work would have been just fine if you hadn't created this chaos by making entryways into my dimension and killing my mentor in the process.
???: Oh, so you noticed our efforts? Our kind has always yearned for total control. Maybe it was out of spite. I mean, all we knew was this empty darkness, so once we got a taste of the light from other dimensions we just couldn't be satiated anymore.
Me: And that led to you going against the former Sustainer?
???: You could say that.
(t): I knew it. All that weird stuff that happened was because of them.
I think back to my first day at work.
(t): They were trying to execute their plan even then, but it seems like the former Sustainer was still interfering.
???: It's true, the former Sustainer was giving us quite some trouble. Even after the wench died, the traps she set for us hindered us for a while. But now that the pest has been dealt with, we are back on track with the plan. Our success is near, I can feel it.
CHOICE OPTION 1: You're getting on my nerves.
(t): How dare they talk so casually about my mentor, the person they murdered ruthlessly.
Me: You claim to want to go the peaceful way, but was it not you who caused a lot of pain by killing the Sustainer of the dimensional Principles? You killed her! You're all murderers!
(t): I never knew her personally, but maybe we are still somehow connected in another way, seeing how emotional I get when she's being disrespected.
???: True, we did dispose of her quite violently. But you must understand, sacrifices for the greater good are inevitable.
My blood starts to boil at this point.
Me: Shut your mouth! Who do you think you are that you get to decide what the greater good is?!
After a little pause the Spirit answers calmly.
CHOICE OPTION 2: Don't worry, I'll find a way.
(t): These Spirits are up to no good. And I promised Scarlet that I'll come back as soon as possible.
Me: You won't be getting anywhere near your goal. I'll make sure of it.
???: Oh?
The voice sounds amused.
???: Pray tell, how will you manage to do that? This realm is not like any other. It is our domain and we have the most control over it. It won't be easy, I've been trying to tell you.
(t): Right, I don't have a plan right now. And that fact is pissing me off.
Me: Argh! Can't you shut up for a second?! Your endless yapping is preventing me from coming up with any ideas!
My outburst makes me feel a little embarrassed.
(t): But nobody is here except that wretched Spirit so it's fine.
Me: The more you talk, the more I want to punch you in your face! I may have never seen it, but I'm sure it's disgusting and ugly. That's why you Spirits need to walk around with those hooded cloaks.
Silence follows my remark and I feel the presence growing colder.
CONTINUE HERE AFTER CHOICE OPTIONS
???: I take that as you declining our proposal?
The voice suddenly sounds deeper and more menacing.
???: Then you leave me no choice. I planned to keep the past and present from mixing, but I'll make an exception for this.
(t): The past and present?
Me: What do you mean?
A bad feeling comes over me and goosebumps spread over my arms.
???: Your lover. There is one person she detests, and he is from the past if I remember correctly?
(t): Scarlet? Is he planning to hurt her now, after all?
Then another thought crosses my mind.
(t): Wait, a person she detests… Amon?!
Me: How do you know Amon?
The bad feeling I noticed earlier turns into fear now and I break out into a cold sweat.
???: That must be the name of the one you fought a little while ago. You see, he seems to have been shifted into the abyssal realm. And he was willing to strike a deal with us, unlike you.
(t): What? Then at that time, I zapped one enemy straight into another enemy's arms???
Guilt and despair creep into my conscience.
(t): Damn it! How could that happen??? I was too preoccupied with Scarlet's condition at that time. I was just glad he was gone.
???: A deal with us is always beneficial for both parties. But you chose to ignore us. Now he will reap the benefits. I will allow him to enter the present, as he wished.
(t): No! He'll hunt Scarlet down and who knows what he'll do to her then.
???: Well, our time here is nearing its end. You won't get out of here so easily, as this realm will soon be destroyed. We won't need it in the new universe. Farewell then.
With that the voice fades away and I can no longer sense its presence.
I'm all alone in this suffocating darkness, panicking over what to do now.
(t): What do I do? Will shifting work?
I try to shift, but for some reason my power won't obey me.
(t): Is it because of this space? What's holding me back?
I feel like I'm slowly going insane after swimming in this darkness for so long.
(t): This isn't good. If this goes on I will slowly lose my sanity and before long the Spirit's plan will be executed and the world we know now will be destroyed.
(t): There must be something I'm able to do! Ugh, sometimes I wish that my mentor was still alive to teach me these things.
(t): But we never got to meet and I'll have to deal with this myself. She trusted me with this duty and believed that I will manage somehow. I just have to believe it too.
